# The right branch of Olmedo et al., TOPLAS 2018, Example 4.9 (p. 4:20): two fair coins (0 is
# heads), observing at least one head; with no loop, cwlp of [y = 0] equals cwp, 2/3.
# Expected: valid.  The reduction is the dual: wp_(1-q)(S, 1 - [y = 0]) <= 1 - q for q = 0.6.
nat x;
nat y;
{
	x := 0;
}[1/2]{
	x := 1;
}
{
	y := 0;
}[1/2]{
	y := 1;
}
observe(x = 0 || y = 0);
?Ex [[y = 0]] >= 0.6 cwlp
